WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:05.230
I- am- an- es-per!

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:11.680
The girl in the spacesuit returned to the game, claiming her super powers made her invincible.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.700
In the end, our shopping district team lost for the second straight game.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.560
The next day...

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.040
What exactly is <i>that?</i>

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.040
Beats me.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.750
The catcher Nakamura-san brought her here, and said she's a relative.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.630
Something about her running away from home, and vandalism on a farm.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.050
Is she really his relative?

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.230
Strike!

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:36.790
What about you, transfer student? What's your deal with <i>that?</i>

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.350
"That"?

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.140
We're cousins.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.270
Oh?

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.640
Does that creep you out?

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:47.650
Slightly.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.610
I only shared a class with that for about two months,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.920
but other girls resented and envied her even before that.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.690
It's that beauty of hers.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.470
Strike! Batter out!

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:08.580
The cousin!

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.340
Step-step-step-step-step!

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:48.890
We lost again.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:51.520
Hanazawa-san pitched a perfect game.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:57.690
We'll probably never escape groundskeeping duty unless she quits that team.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:01.530
Good work. I brought sandwiches today.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.410
Um, Maekawa-san...

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.790
What is it now?

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:09.370
Well, I just wanted to thank you again.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:13.070
I haven't been playing well at all, but you still bring lunches for me.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:14.040
That makes me really happy.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.590
As expected of our womanizing transfer student!

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:25.010
Um, a certain word in that sentence shouldn't really be there.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:27.890
More importantly, aren't you going to save her?

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:37.940
"S-a-v-e m-e, c-o-u-s-i-n."

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.210
Ow!

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:02.050
Hand- her- o-ver, she's- an- a-li-en!

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.010
Ex-alien, and self-proclaimed!

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.220
<i>It's- a-</i> one- of- us!

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.060
Don't randomly mix English in.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:13.900
As- fell-ow- a-li-ens, we- should- get- a-long.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:16.940
What? Wasn't being an esper your backstory?

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.480
That has nothing to do with being an alien.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:22.820
And- al-so- an- a-li-en.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.530
That's a half-assed setup.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.030
It's not a setup, damn it!

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.080
I'm- the- real- thing.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.700
Actually, I heard you ran away.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:31.830
Go home.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.330
I- came- for- bu-si-ness.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.880
You- dumb-ass.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:44.840
I- don't- rea-lly- care, but- they- forced- me- to...

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.930
Where did you really come from?

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:47.970
I said spac—

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.720
I- said- space.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.060
Hey, you.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.730
What, dumb-ass?

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.820
You don't have to return to space,

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:01.230
your common sense is already out of this world!

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:06.660
Why, you! You- don't- bel-ieve- me- at- all!

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.030
You should speak normally now.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:10.490
You're starting to run out of breath.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.920
Learn to get rid of that thing by yourself.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.250
I-I don't have my futon on.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:22.050
You should only rely on the futon for sleeping.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:23.880
Th-Then...

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.590
I'll rely on the cousin.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:29.930
Y-You already do.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.520
Yes, so I'll rely on you even more.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.690
The cousin's arm is cold.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.860
That's just my sweat, cooling off.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:47.820
Are you practicing in the park?

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.700
Nakajima didn't show up today.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.830
An ex-boyfriend, or...?

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.710
In secret training.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.800
Can I come watch?

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:08.380
I will be waiting with anticipation.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.300
Is Touwa-san coming too?

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:14.930
Suppose she did.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:18.270
Would that upset you?

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.610
Touwa-san and I get along very well,

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.360
so I think that would be great.

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:31.070
But something suddenly came up,

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:33.530
so I don't think I can see you today.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:37.370
Hey, did you have fun playing baseball?

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.290
So-so.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:42.170
I see.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.670
When I get back, I'll take a nap 'til noon.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:50.590
Espers should just get on bikes and return to space.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:56.680
But they can't, so everyone's stuck here as nothing but self-proclaimed aliens.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.850
Stuck forever, in this city.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:06.110
The cousin...

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.150
Ni-Niwa-kun!

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:10.150
What?

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:12.160
The cousin's name... Niwa.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:15.160
That's right, but what's going on?

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.040
Niwa-kun...

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.410
Are you imitating Ryuushi-san?

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:22.000
Did you think of a weird backstory?

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.170
It's not a backstory, damn it!

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.040
Probably.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:32.840
Well, well, well.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.640
If it isn't the dumbass!

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.890
Why are you here?

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.520
There are nice eaves here, so I couldn't resist.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.810
The Earthlings slept in cramped shelters like this,

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:45.230
in their spaceship when they visited our planet.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:48.440
When in Rome...

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.700
Do you have some business here?

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.660
If you do, please ring the front doorbell!

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:01.750
I'm just a lone alien looking for shelter. Don't mind me.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:05.630
You think I can just ignore a suspicious runaway or farm vandal or whatever?

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.000
Such a skeptic!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.840
With that personality of yours,

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:13.220
you'll probably never encounter a paranormal phenomenon.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:16.180
Huh? I just realized you're talking normally.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:19.970
I used up my esper mana speaking the alien language.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.100
Oh, your throat dried out?

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:28.730
I merely decided it'd be wasted on a non-believer who denies the existence of espers and aliens.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:32.700
What's this?

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:33.360
Sumakin.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.200
You think you can beat me with that simple armament?

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:39.990
I'm Meteor level in terms of Time Magic,

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:43.250
RockThrow level in terms of Special Attack!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:50.760
What's that?

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.510
A telescope!

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:56.510
Tele— You're interested in the stars? Which one of you?

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:10.650
Hey!

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:16.360
It was like seeing a fixed star emitting light in all directions.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:23.040
This night may turn out to be the real beginning of this summer.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:27.460
You bitch!

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.540
Are you aware that by laying a finger on me,

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:34.170
you've just shortened your lifespan to the end of this summer?

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:36.800
Do you even know who I am?

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:41.890
Oh well, you're a fellow Dannari.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:43.430
I will forgive you.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.850
Seeing The Cousin's inappropriate attitude,

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:51.150
I can sympathize with you. I'll let this one slide.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:54.780
Wait. I don't remember becoming your relative.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:58.320
Huh? Your name isn't "The Cousin"?

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:00.450
No, I'm Niwa Makoto.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:01.160
What?

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:04.500
That's strange, I'm certain she called you that.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:08.670
I wasn't very enthused about this job, but I'm sure I heard...

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:10.500
Never mind.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:13.460
I forgot to tell you.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:16.010
My name is Hoshimiya Yashiro.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:18.880
A genuine esper and an alien!

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:22.510
My stay on this planet is for business, not pleasure.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:23.930
Don't you forget that!

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:33.070
Open up, damn it!

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.570
The cousin...

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:36.190
Don't worry.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:38.150
It's best not to get involved with that type.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.530
What's your problem?

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.410
She finally gave up.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:46.700
Well then, good night.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.920
Herro herro, is this Niwa-kun?

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.800
And you are Ryuushi-san.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.300
It's Ryuuko!

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.300
Oh! It's the real Ryuushi-san!

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.050
It's Ryuuko!

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:04.930
It is!

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.180
What is it?

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:10.310
My eyes are wide open, and I can't sleep.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:12.310
Did you take a really long nap?

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:15.860
What's with that dreamless imagination?

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:17.900
Can't sleep, so no dream.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.570
Did Ryuuko-san just say something funny?

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:20.950
Clap, clap, clap.

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:23.410
Thank you, thank you.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:26.580
Actually, I'm really nervous right now, in two ways.

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:30.210
It's what they call "double meaning", you know.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:34.460
I was about to criticize the misuse of that term,
but I got too distracted by your cute sentence ender!

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:37.590
I bit my tongue! Ow...

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:39.840
What are you nervous about?

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.970
Um... you know.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:44.970
We're talking on the phone for the very first time.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:47.100
Oh, right.

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.390
I'm totally panicked!

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:52.690
It's like you're right there by my ear.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:54.610
Doesn't that make you go "whoa"?

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:57.110
Well, I guess.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:59.900
And the other reason is...

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:03.110
there's a basketball game next week.

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:05.620
Oh, I think I'll go, as promised.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.740
That <i>is</i> the problem!

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:10.870
Oh, by the way,

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:14.630
sorry about this morning. Something urgent came up.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:18.630
I don't mind. Anyway, what's the problem?

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:24.890
Actually, I wanted to practice until I could say "it's perfect!",

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:28.310
then call you after I knew I'd be playing in the game.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:31.560
But that might not be before graduation, let alone the end of summer!

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:33.020
That was what I was panicking about.

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:34.770
I don't think it really matters.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:37.520
But you know, if I call you to the game,

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:40.150
and then I don't get to play...

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:43.030
Oh, I see what you mean.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:46.200
I'll pray for you, then, that Ryuushi-san gets to play.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:50.740
I'd rather have you cheer for me.

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:52.660
Prayer is for God,

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:55.830
but cheering would send your voice directly to me.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:57.460
And it's Ryuuko!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.460
If I get to play,

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.800
and "Ryuuko-chan is unstoppable!",

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.640
if I play that well,

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:09.180
then maybe I'll expect some kind of reward!

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:11.350
Just kidding.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.980
As long as it's a wish within my powers.

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:16.230
Well, then...

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:20.480
How about going to the summer festival together?

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:21.610
Summer festival?

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:26.990
Yeah. It's kind of lame visiting all the booths by myself at this age.

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:30.490
That's more like a reward for me!

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:31.580
Huh?

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:35.000
Nothing. When's the summer festival? Is it in this city?

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:40.090
Yeah, the biggest one is in mid-August!

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:41.000
Oh...

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.340
Niwa-kun, you play amateur baseball and you didn't know that?

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:52.100
Whoever wins the last game each year decides which side of the city gets to run the festival.

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:53.850
If the city side wins,

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:56.810
the shopping district has less participation,

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:58.310
and vice versa.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:00.230
That's what my dad told me.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:03.440
So we were playing practice games before the real thing.

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:07.570
Speaking of baseball, about Nakajima-kun...

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:09.990
Yeah, what is it?

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:15.370
Nakajima-kun is the person I asked out before, and he turned me down.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:19.420
Oh, really? That's too bad.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:20.380
For who?

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.590
For Nakajima.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:25.800
Then, if I asked you...

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:27.880
Huh? What did you say?

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.760
Nothing!

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:36.140
Good morn—

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:37.640
Morning, Mako-rin!

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:42.150
Who's the girl who's even weirder than the way you just greeted me?

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:43.770
Mako-kun, Mako-kun...

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:45.780
Oh, no.

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:51.120
I found her passed out under the eaves when I went out to hang up the laundry.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:52.410
I was sleeping.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.700
So I kept her!

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:59.790
Don't laugh together, don't be on the same wavelength... and don't keep her!

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:04.040
Why did you let her into the house?

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:09.050
I-It's not because she called me "onee-san"!

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:13.260
Meme is a nice person.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:17.020
I only reward and save people I like.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:20.850
Me too! I saved you because I like you!

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:23.480
I see.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:29.360
She doesn't appear to understand what it means to be an alien.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:32.110
It seems she doesn't have what it takes to be one of us.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.200
You're done with chasing her around?

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:38.290
The cause is unknown, so further investigation is necessary, but...

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.210
I don't feel like it.

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:41.000
Ah.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.750
Now then, I'm going to continue with my laundry.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.300
Are you sure you're fine with this?

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:52.340
What's the problem? It feels like having a little sister.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:54.550
Right, right. You're so carefree.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:56.510
I have a personal reason for it.

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:57.430
Oh?

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:00.140
She reminds me of Elliott when he was little.

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:02.440
So I couldn't help but be nice to her.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:07.980
For some reason, I ended up taking Yashiro home.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:09.440
Where does she live anyway?

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:11.280
Are you sure I can keep it?

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:12.240
Sure.

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:13.200
I'm not giving it back.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.910
I said I gave it to you!

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:16.370
You won't get anything back in return.

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:19.950
If I expected something back in return, I would've given it to someone else.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.040
What do you mean by that?

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.580
Exactly what it sounds like.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:26.540
I won't inflict my super powers on you.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.210
Thanks.

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.300
Stop staring!

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:36.430
The next time you see the sun at night,
that's the end of your life!

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:39.180
That wouldn't be night.

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:46.150
Here we are.

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:51.860
Wh-What's- this- dump- with-out- eaves?

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:53.900
Eaves set the standard?

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:56.570
What? Wan-na- fight?

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:08.090
You've- lost- be-cause- you- have- been- li-ving- a- sof-tie- life- on- this- pla-net!

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:12.710
The cousin, are you going to see Granny?

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:15.680
Hmm... I'll go see her later.

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:18.140
Okay! Granny will be happy to see you.

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:19.010
Are you sure?

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:21.810
I am. She likes the cousin.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.140
I'm off to work!

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.770
Okay, work hard!

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:33.110
I have to let you know, my bicycle doesn't fly.

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:35.990
As if I expected such high-dimensional hospitality from you.

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:38.870
There's somewhere I want to go.
I'll give you directions, you just pedal.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:40.450
We just have to go there?

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:42.580
Yeah, I'll let—

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.250
I'll- let- you- off- the- hook.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.290
Gee, thanks.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:49.460
Hey.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:50.380
What?

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:51.920
Why don't you take the helmet off?

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.590
I'm sealing in my super powers with it.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:57.300
It can't be carelessly taken off.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:01.390
You seriously believe in super powers?

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:03.720
You don't, right?

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:05.730
Then what's the point in asking? You fool.

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:08.270
You don't shy away from throwing in insults, do you?

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:12.440
I'm tired of trying to convince you with words.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.900
Everyone on this planet is the same.

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:17.010
They blindly deny the existence of paranormal phenomena,

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:18.660
insisting they can't possibly exist.

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:20.530
Turn right.

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:24.620
Believing is the first step.

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:27.960
Would believing actually change anything?

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:31.880
Physical forces aren't the only forces moving the universe.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:37.380
Maybe you're here now only because you casually kicked a pebble in the past.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:39.550
The theory with butterfly's wings or something?

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:43.720
It's the truth about the extent of human powers.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:47.230
At the same time, there is the possibility of human beings as the cause of paranomal phenome—

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:48.980
Stop! Stop!

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:51.690
No, wait, I can't!

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:54.860
That was dangerous, you idiot!

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.440
It's a pond!

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.360
No, that's a pool.

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:09.830
Hey! Is this our destination?

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:10.830
Yes!

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:13.880
Earthlings are only smart when it comes to things like this!

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.420
Who would've thought of making a pond with cold water?

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:34.310
Well, I'm going.

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.820
Leave before someone catches you in there.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:47.200
My heart almost stopped! Literally!

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:48.080
Huh?

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:49.710
Wait a minute...

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:52.790
She did it from that distance? Without a bucket?

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:57.590
Lucky you. It doesn't look like super powers are needed to enter the pond.

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:02.800
Join me. Turn on your brain once in a while.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:03.930
Don't leave it switched off forever.

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:08.850
Damn it, I'm still hot, and she's having such a good time in there!

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:11.020
Turn your brain on, and grow up!

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:14.440
Realize that you don't have to give up on things you can do, dumbass!

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:17.570
Fine.

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:25.280
Geronimo!

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:51.310
As- I- thought, Ma-ko-to- has- the- po-ten-tial!

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:53.690
Give me a break!

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:58.020
Take this! Kamehameha!

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:58.690
That's cold!

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:04.570
Hey!

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.570
Are you sure I can leave you here?

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:09.410
Yes. Thank you.

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:16.540
See ya.

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:27.050
Yo. Why aren't you looking after the shop?

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:30.390
No one's coming in, so... I'm trying to attract some business?

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:32.390
Oh? Any progress?

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.020
I have captured the cousin.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:37.940
Did you change your head?

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:39.560
I can't just replace it!

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:40.940
I made a mistake.

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:42.190
Did you change your hair?

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:44.190
It's still wet.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.280
Wet? Did it rain?

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:47.530
I jumped into a pool.

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:50.120
I'm jealous.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.660
I like pools more than the sea.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:53.910
Are you telling me to take you next time?

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:54.910
Yes, yes!

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.370
I'll take you when I have time.

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:59.210
Let's go, Granny's waiting.

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:00.340
Okay.

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:03.170
Erio.

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:06.930
You're a little suntanned.

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:10.010
Yep!

00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:44.400
Maekawa-san's sandwich, and early morning baseball: +2

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:46.570
Getting involved with a girl in a spacesuit: -2

00:23:46.570 --> 00:23:48.400
Getting involved again at night: -2

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:50.490
First phone conversation with Ryuushi-san: +1

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.240
Yashiro invades the Touwa home: -2

00:23:53.240 --> 00:23:55.740
Illegally jumping into the school's pool: +3

00:23:55.740 --> 00:23:58.040
Current adolescence points total: +6

00:23:58.040 --> 00:24:03.540
Next time: This Year's Summer is Basketball and Super Powers and Futon and Stargazing and Summer Festival and Baseball and...

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:04.500
And Meme-tan!

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:05.670
Don't barge in!

00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:09.010
Meme-chin is lonely without Mako-kun lately!
